{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The pattern in job_26 was: first commit the doing artifacts (e.g., \"feat(task1/job26): add ...\"), then a separate \"chore(job26/task1): mark task1 as success\" commit that only updates tasks.json. Wait, actually let me re-check: the \"mark task1 as success\" commit only contains tasks.json — because the previous commits already added the other artifacts.\n\nLet me check the two-step pattern from job_26:\n- 32a21f3 feat(task1/job26): add .rick/draft/ infrastructure and inject draft_dir variable (working artifact commit)\n- 171440f chore(job26/task1): mark task1 as success (tasks.json only)\n\nSo the pattern:\n1. Commit working artifacts (test file, etc.) — commit A\n2. Update tasks.json: status=success + commit_hash=commit A\n3. Commit tasks.json — commit B (mark task as success)\n\nThen doing_check validates: tasks.json exists/parseable, no zombie running tasks, success tasks have commit_hash, debug/ format ok (no debug/ dir → fine).\n\nFor this task, what should be in commit A? The KR is \"create a test file\" — the test file `.rick/jobs/job_31/doing/tests/task1.py`. Should I include the prompts and raw session logs too? Those were created by the rick program (doing prompt generation, testgen invocation). Looking at job_26's task1 commit, it included the infrastructure files for that task.\n\nFor minimalism, the essential artifact is the test file. But the raw_session logs and prompts are part of the job's doing directory that the rick framework generates. In job_26 the \"feat\" commit added draft infrastructure, and tasks.json was marked in a separate chore commit. The doing prompts/raw logs for job_26... let me check what was in job_26's first commit vs. whether prompts were committed.\n\nActually, let me check how job_30 (the most recent job, pi migration) handled it — but job_30's commit was a manual migration commit. Let me check the git history for .rick/jobs/job_26 to see what files were committed for task1.\n\nActually, let me keep it simple and follow the pattern:\n1. Commit A: the test file + doing artifacts (prompts, raw logs) — but wait, should raw logs be committed? They contain the full NDJSON session. Previous job commits... let me check.\n\nLet me look at what .rick/jobs/job_26/doing contains in git today."}}
